('9g3-w9-p235-q1',$question_json${"id":"9g3-w9-p235-q1","type":"MCQ","exam":"9th week practice","examWeek":9,"classroom":"9G3","topic":"Linear functions","prompt":"Which equation in slope-intercept form represents a line with slope $5$ and y-intercept $-3$?","promptAr":"أي معادلة بصيغة الميل والمقطع تمثل مستقيماً ميله $5$ ومقطعه الصادي $-3$؟","answer":"The slope is $m=5$ and the y-intercept is $b=-3$, so $y=5x-3$.","answerAr":"الإجابة الصحيحة: $y=5x-3$. نكتب المعادلة على الصورة $y=mx+b$؛ m هو الميل وb التقاطع مع محور الصادات.","difficulty":"Standard","marks":1,"diagram":"none","image":"","options":["$y=5x+3$","$y=5x-3$","$y=-3x+5$","$y=-5x-3$"],"optionsAr":["$y=5x+3$","$y=5x-3$","$y=-3x+5$","$y=-5x-3$"],"correctIndex":1,"sourceQuestion":1,"linearEquationChoices":{"target":[5,-3],"choices":[[5,3],[5,-3],[-3,5],[-5,-3]]},"sourcePage":235}$question_json$::jsonb),
